.TH APPROX 1 approx\-VERSION
.SH NAME
approx \- non-interactive POSIX fuzzy stream filter and ranker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B approx
.RB [ \-isveV ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR threshold ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR count ]
.I pattern
.RI [ file\ ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B approx
is a stream filter and ranker that scores lines against a fuzzy search
.I pattern
using normalized approximate string distance. It is designed for POSIX
pipelines, shell scripts, and resource-constrained embedded systems.
.P
If no
.I file
operands are specified, or if a file operand is
.BR \- ,
.B approx
reads from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t " threshold"
Minimum similarity threshold between
.B 0.00
and
.B 1.00
required for a line to match. Default is
.BR 0.70 .
.TP
.BI \-n " count"
Rank and output only the top
.I count
lines with the highest similarity score.
.TP
.B \-s
Prepend the similarity score and a tab character before each matching line.
.TP
.B \-i
Match case-insensitively.
.TP
.B \-v
Invert the sense of matching, selecting non-matching lines (similarity score below threshold).
.TP
.B \-e
Perform exact full-line Levenshtein distance comparison rather than finding the best matching substring.
.TP
.B \-V
Print version information to standard output and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
At least one matching line was selected.
.TP
.B 1
No lines were selected.
.TP
.B >1
An error occurred (invalid arguments, unreadable file, out of memory).
.SH EXAMPLES
Filter log lines tolerating typos in "connection timeout":
.IP
.EX
cat server.log | approx "connection timeout"
.EE
.P
Find the top 5 closest matches with their scores from a wordlist:
.IP
.EX
approx -n 5 -s "recieve" /usr/share/dict/words
.EE
.P
Case-insensitive search with a strict 85% threshold:
.IP
.EX
dmesg | approx -i -t 0.85 "out of memory"
.EE
